nd expert ratings.", "Incumbent Derek Tran (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Incumbent Democrat Derek Tran faces Republican Chuong Vo in California's redrawn 45th District, a seat with a modest Democratic lean. Tran has raised roughly $5.8 million and holds $3.2 million on hand, dwarfing Vo's $844,000 raised and $296,000 in the bank, and outside spending on either side has been minimal so far. Ten expert ratings place the race between Likely D and Safe D, and prediction markets give Tran about a 93-94 percent chance of winning.\n\nNo public general-election polls are available, so the outlook rests on fundamentals: the district's Democratic lean, Tran's incumbency and financial dominance, and a favorable national environment. Campaign coverage has centered on immigration and housing, with both Vietnamese American candidates discussing their family histories in immigration policy. The race sits firmly on the Democratic side of the ledger, though the absence of polling leaves some room for surprise.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9684, "margin": 12.49}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9556, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9612, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.946, "margin": 11.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9456, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9427, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.958, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9598, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9517, "margin": 11.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9635, "margin": 11.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.956, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9567, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9608, "margin": 12.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9408, "margin": 11.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9446, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.9604, "margin": 12.5}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.9544, "margin": 11.0}, {"date"